  READ THIS BEFORE IMPORTING:
    * The four wheel joints are `continuous` and MUST be velocity-driven. A position
      target on a continuous joint fails in PhysX past +/-2*pi of accumulated
      command. Use the two actuator groups in whelp16_actuators.py.
    * Wheel collision is a <cylinder> primitive on purpose. Do not let the importer
      replace it with a convex hull of the tire mesh; that is what wheel chatter is.
    * All meshes are millimetre-authored and carry scale="0.001 0.001 0.001".
    * Effort limits are the servo's STALL torque. Its CONTINUOUS rating is a third of
      that (0.98 N.m). A policy that lives near the effort
      limit will cook twelve servos in an afternoon; penalise torque and action rate.
-->
